	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Zellij Sessions

Type `zj` (configurable) to list sessions. Running sessions come first, then exited ones.

| Key | Running session | Exited session |
|-----|-----------------|----------------|
| ↩ | Focus / switch / attach | Resurrect |
| ⌥↩ | Kill (stays resurrectable) | Delete |
| ⌃↩ | Rename | – |
| fn↩ | Open in a new Ghostty window | Open in a new Ghostty window |
| ⇧ / ⌘Y | Quick Look of the active pane | – |

**Opening a session** focuses the Ghostty terminal already showing it. Otherwise it switches the Zellij client in the frontmost Ghostty terminal. If no terminal can be switched, it opens a new Ghostty window.

**Creating**: type a name that does not exist and press ↩. Add `@` to pick a layout, e.g. `zj api @compact`. Press ⌥↩ to create in the background.

**Deleting a running session** takes two steps: ⌥↩ kills it and the list reopens with it marked as exited; ⌥↩ again deletes it. No actions use ⌘, because Alfred itself uses ⌘.

**Bulk**: type `kill all` or `delete all`.

Requires Ghostty 1.3+ (AppleScript) and Zellij 0.44+.</string>
